the so-called water tank of morocco the  middle atlas mountain range is  experiencing an unprecedented long  absence of snow complicating the  repercussions of a severe drought that  could impact the crop-importing nations  the slopes of mitchell finn's ski resort  and the habri mount region have not seen  snow for up to three and a half months  during their winter season this means  that rivers sourcing their water from  this northern region may not be able to  feed farms that are as far as 200 miles  away  the kingdom has pledged 1.1 billion in  aid for farmers who account for  one-third of the active workforce to  help them mitigate the repercussions of  the most severe drought to hit morocco  since 1981  the absence of snow has also affected  tourism in the area  there are far less tourists and school  trips for the resorts  foreign  locals believe morocco's water problems  will most likely get worse before they  get better as water intensive farming  lower precipitation and the effects of  climate change combined could further  reduce the kingdom's water capital  [Music]
 

